# The virtual environment install.bat builds. Machine-local by nature:
# a venv hardcodes the absolute path it was created at.
.venv/
docs/

# Learned data and local state
userdata/
calib.json
Start Helpermon.bat
Start bot.bat
Bot starten.bat

# The images the board bots read the screen with. They are crops from the
# game, so they were held back here for a long time -- and that left the
# Digital World Search bot unusable in a published copy, because a fresh
# install has no userdata folder and nothing to fall back on. They ship now,
# on purpose. Everything else from the game screen stays out: the debug
# dumps below, and anything under userdata.

# Debug output, and the screenshots posted for features still to be built.
# One folder per bot and no more -- debug_dungeon, debug_explore,
# debug_skewer, debug_summon, debug_quest, debug_passive -- named after the
# module the bot lives in, plus debug_UI for the launcher, the wizard, About
# and Feedback. A folder per feature was tried first and grew nine of them,
# four holding one or two pictures each, and a frame of the Explore menu was
# then looked for in the wrong one. debug-queue stays the inbox: what has
# just been posted, and what belongs to a bot nobody has written yet.
# All of it is pictures from the game screen, so none of it belongs in the
# repository. Matched by prefix rather than named one by one, the rule
# release.py already builds by, so a folder made in a hurry needs nobody to
# remember this file: debug_UI was the one that got through.
debug*/
*.log

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Internal working documents. They stay on this machine: CLAUDE.md is the
# rulebook for working on the code, RELEASE_PLAN.md the running plan, and
# neither belongs in a published copy. release.py already holds both back
# from a build; this keeps them out of the repository as well.
CLAUDE.md
RELEASE_PLAN.md
GITHUB_ROLLOUT.md
